From: q2q port
Subject: [PATCH] q2q: skip the precautionary CNTP_CTL_EL0 write on SWEET

On the Galaxy Z Fold3 (SM8350) the hypervisor traps EL1 access to the ARM
physical timer, so _enable_virtual_timer()'s 'MSR CNTP_CTL_EL0' raises an
undefined-instruction exception (panic in _fiq_context_init+0x14). SWEET only
uses the virtual timer (CNTV, INTID 19), so the write is skipped there.

---
diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
--- a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
@@ -2274,7 +2274,9 @@
 
 	__builtin_arm_wsr64("CNTV_CTL_EL0", cntvctl);
 	/* disable the physical timer as a precaution, as its registers reset to architecturally unknown values */
+#if !defined(SWEET) /* q2q/SM8350: EL1 physical-timer access traps (UNDEF); timer runs on CNTV */
 	__builtin_arm_wsr64("CNTP_CTL_EL0", CNTP_CTL_EL0_IMASKED);
+#endif
 }
 
 void
